WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.370
Gatwick Airport, December 2018.

2
00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.850
Flights are grounded.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.250
The shutdown lasts almost 36 hours.

4
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:13.730
In the House of Commons Library's words,
several thousands of passengers are disrupted.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:18.350
Something had shut the airport, and the
state could not simply switch it off.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.290
Why not?

7
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.630
Was it heavy snow?

8
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.850
A strike by air traffic controllers?

9
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.310
In this mission, you'll meet
disruptive technologies:

10
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.690
innovations that change
how things are made,

11
00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.310
moved or done.

12
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:35.930
Then you'll test a 2017 projection that 3D
printing could wipe out almost one-quarter

13
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:40.370
of world trade by 2060, if
investment in printers keeps growing,

14
00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:43.170
and ask what that means for sovereignty.

15
00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:47.930
Your mission: explain why the state
couldn't simply stop what grounded Gatwick's

16
00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:48.670
flights.
